  "reasoning": "The patient presents with fever, headache, swollen lymph nodes, weakness, and fatigue. Swollen lymph nodes are a classic sign of the immune system actively fighting an infection. While several conditions on the list involve fever and fatigue, they typically include more specific distinguishing symptoms: malaria usually features prominent chills, heavy sweating, and muscle pain; dengue commonly presents with pain behind the eyes, joint/muscle pain, and rashes; typhoid is characterized by persistent abdominal pain and bowel changes; and allergies typically cause sneezing, itchy/watery eyes, and nasal congestion without significant fever or lymphadenopathy. The combination of fever, headache, generalized weakness/fatigue, and swollen lymph nodes strongly aligns with a viral upper respiratory infection. Therefore, the most accurate diagnosis from the provided options is the common cold.",
